Generally a segment can be considered any section of a network that can be
easily isolated.

Others consider a segment to consist of  a "collision domain" for ethernet.

Because of the nature of how ethernet works, you can have a network cable on
the brink of total failure and most if not all systems on it can appear to
be happy.

Only with network monitoring tools or by watching the network counters on
the various devices that you might have a clue that there is a problem.

Just because only one device is having a problem, does not totally exonerate
the network configuration.

But I agree with you that it is not likely that the network is the problem.
It is just after replacing the VAX processor and bulkhead did not fix the
