A VAX 4000-200, VAX 4000-300, VAX 4000-500 may be able to work at 5.4-2,
some of them may need a manditory ECO.

Also some of the VAX 4000 processors will require minimum revisions of some
of the Q-BUS boards.  I am assuming that the faster VAX processors uncovered
some timing irregularities.  How this will affect your third party Q-BUS
cards can not be predicted.

What you need to find is the S.P.D. for VAX/VMS 5.4-2.

If you are not dependent on it having an imbedded ethernet controller, a use
VAX 3500 or 3800 processor, memory, and either a DELQA, or a DESQA(sp?) may
also be substituted.

It may be cheaper for you to find a used VAX with all of the above than to
just purchase the parts :-)

