the front panel  (the shiny metal bit containing the ethernet, console
connections etc) that can cause ethernet to fail sporadically or
completely. Costs about 300 dollars for a replacement from field
service. I've seen this fail on three or four machines over the last
ten years, Some of the ethernet logic is on the cpu board but I have
never seen this fail - just the front panel which does contain a small
amount of active components. I'd tend to supsect this.

