> Also, I think there were some changes to device driver architecture since
5.4,
> so source code changes might be needed.  I don't know for sure.

The source code is effectively unavailable except at great effort and pos-
sibly expense.  Ditto someone to make any needed source changes.  It's very
unlikely that my client can afford to pay for either.  However, I'll
dutifully
remind him that "given sufficiently large amounts of money, very little is
impossible."

> Someone will certainly need to obtain and read the intervening release
> notes to see if there is a potential problem with the driver.

We'll cross that bridge if-and-when we come to it -- but thanks for pointing
out this necessity.  I probably wouldn't have thought of it.

> Vax 4000 series machines are nice, and they have Q-bus.

Now THAT is a VERY GOOD IDEA.  This product used to run, as-is (no driver
changes!) on 4000 series machines.  I'll definitely suggest that.

