That's very interesting!  If this is a commonplace problem it makes it
just barely possible for both the "original" and the "replacement" CPUs
to have the SAME problem, as we're observing.

(A couple of sub-respondents have since been discussing with Alan the
details of the problem, and the procedure/simplicity of removing-and-
replacing the panel from the CPU card.  I won't delve into that here.)

What I could REALLY use at this point is a source of this part in the
US (Rochester, NY to be specific) and a part number or a source of that
information.  Anyone?

