helbig@astro.rug.nl (Phillip Helbig) writes:
>VAXStation 4000 90
>
>KA49-A V1.0-006-V4.0
>08-00-2B-10-6E-C9
>64 MB
>|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||
>?? 001   2      LCSPX  0512
>
>>>> sh dev
>
>VMS/VMB    ADDR    DEVTYPE    NUMBYTES   RM/FX   WP   DEVNAM   REV   
>______     ____    _______    ________   ____    __   ______   ___
>EZA0       08-00-2B-10-6E-C9
>DKA0       A/0/0   DISK       426.25MB   FX           RZ25     0900
>...HostID.. A7      INITR
>
>Does the following look normal?
>
>What about the ??---something to worry about?
>
>What does the RM/FX mean?

The double "?" usually means that there was a hard error for that device.
The LCSPX is the video card, but without the manual I can not tell you
which error you have.  The RM/FX is ReMovable/FiXed for the SCSI drives
on the bus.  A tape or CD-Rom would be removable, while the hard drive is
fixed or non-removable.

