In article <8siljp$eok$1@info.service.rug.nl>, helbig@astro.rug.nl (Phillip Helbig) writes:
>It seems that one needs to use the socket with the two arrows on the 
>terminal and the one with the picture of the printer on the VAX.  

If the VS31xx is in alternate console mode (via S3 switch), the
connector with the printer icon becomes the console port.
At power up some tests are running and some output is written to
this port. 9600,N,8,1
So, yes.
But is alternate console mode enabled on your machine ?
Have you tried both settings of the S3 switch (only read on power-up !) ?

>                                                           If the 
>arrows are used on the VAX (and on the terminal), then the power-up 
>screen on the VT gets erased, but none of the messages reach the screen. 

Which messages ? VAX messages ?

Until VMS is booted, no output is written to this serial line
(maybe except a break or NUL during controller initialization) and to
the other serial line if the graphic console is in use.

And VMS only writes something to this lines, if you added some code
(like $ REPLY/ALL "You may login now") to the VMS startup or tried
to login on this line via a return, ^C, ^Y or similar from the attached
device.

>If the printer socket is used on the terminal, regardless of which is 
>used on the VAX, the power-up screen remains.

The terminal printer socket on the terminal is for a printer attached
to the terminal. You will not want to use this port for the connection
to the VAX !

>Can anyone provide a brief explanation as to WHY this is the case?

If it's still not clear, you may ask again later.

>Any reason to prefer an RS232?

No. The VAXstation printer port is DEC423. If you want the alternate
console functionality, you need this port. So DEC423 is the way to go.

>Is the preferred console-terminal setting data leads only (as opposed to 
>modem control), receive=transmit=9600, XOFF at 64, 8 bits no parity, one 
>stop bit, no local echo, disconnect 2 s delay, unlimited transmit, no 
>auto answerback, not concealed?

Modem control is not useful on DEC423. Switch it off.

