moroney@world.std.spaamtrap.com (Michael Moroney) writes:

>I'll check again the system at work tomorrow, but ones I remember that do
>are LAT, MOP, the SYSID/remote console protocol (the last 2 are by LANCP),
>LAST, NI-SCS, and a couple others I don't remember offhand.  DECnet and
>UCX do not have the change address attribute.  This means that UCX has to
>be started after DECnet but the others can be started at any time.

In case anyone cares ...

Protocols with the "can change address" attribute ON are:

SCA (NI clustering)
DNAME (twice, Ethernet protocol and 802E protocol)
DTIME
PATHWRK
AMDS
LAST
LAT

Ones that don't are:
DECNETV
DECNET (IV)
IP
ARP (part of TCPIP)
86-DD (also part of TCPIP)
BIOS

-Mike


