> Now, another dumb question... how do I translate these above values to
> switch/jumper settings on the TKQ50 for secondary controller use?

OK. The numbers are all in octal (all these busses started in the 
PDP-11 era).

So 760404 is 111 110 000 100 000 100
I posted the card details the other day so deja should
be able to dig it up. Basically there is a row of jumpers
(ignore the switchpacks) that set A12 down to A2 (A17:A13
are fixed at 1, A1:A0 are both 0). A jumper installed is a 1
otherwise its a zero.

For the above you need A8 and A2 installed and the rest out
(I think ...) The vector is set properly by the system.
A2 is the jumper nearest the edge of the card (i.e.
travel left into the card to go towards A12).

