Hi,

I was wondering if anyone out there still has access to the old DEC
Professional magazines.

I am a college instructor with a somewhat unusual request. 

About 1992, RAXCO ran an ad campaign using cartoons drawn by the late 
Don Martin.  These ads ran in the DEC Professional and similar (I 
assume) magazines. 

I teach operating systems and we discuss many of the concepts lampooned 
in the cartoons ("Head Crashes are Bad for Your System", "Fragmentation 
Happens"...).  I would like to use the images from these ads in my class 
notes, but I don't have the original ads.  I have no access to old 
copies of the magazines. 

RAXCO will give me the copyright if there is any way I can obtain could
copies of these ads in electronic (or hardcopy) format.  RAXCO does not
have the ads in any old files.

Thanks for your time, 
        Randy 

