From time to time, I've posted (or responded to) messages involving used 
hardware.  I've managed to give some things a good home which otherwise 
would have been thrown out.  I also bought a few things used, but at the 
moment have to spend my money on other things.  :-(  Sometimes, I get 
LOTS of responses (also when I give stuff away---often, people want the 
whole lot to go at once, so I take things I don't want and hold them 
until I find a good home (I once had 12 responses from people wanting a 
PDP 11!)), sometimes none at all.

It looks like I will have to leave research, at least temporarily, due 
to financial reasons (no, it's not my passion for all things 
|d|i|g|i|t|a|l| which is costing me, but several one-off costs which 
unfortunately hit me at the same time).  Now, I have my machines at work 
for research purposes, and hobbyist machines at home (hopefully soon to 
be connected to the internet).  If I'm not in a position to run my own 
VMS machines (and do more or less what I want with them) at my next 
place of employment, I will have to move my "research" cluster to my 
"permanent" home in Germany (I want to keep it separate from the 
hobbyist cluster so that I can easily move it somewhere else if 
necessary) and have some sort of minimal system to lug about to wherever 
I am living while working at my new job (which might be contract work 
and thus change location relatively often), so that I can a) work 
locally and b) log in to my stuff at my "permanent" residence.

Thus, I'm looking for new hardware---both because I need more per se, 
and also because, if the stuff might be running for a while while I am 
somewhere else, I would like a greater degree of redundancy.  In 
decreasing order of importance, this is what I need:

   o  any type of SCSI disks (1 GB or more), preferably in SBBs

   o  any type of SCSI CD-ROMs, preferably in SBBs

   o  any type of SCSI DAT (but accepting 90-m tapes) or DLT drives

   o  any ALPHA machines 

   o  any desktop VAX machines which are not too slow (VAXstation 
      3100 M76 or better)

   o  InfoServer mounting brackets

   o  hardware documentation (on paper) for anything I might have

At the moment, I could collect from anywhere in the Netherlands or 
northern Germany.  When I can range farther afield again, I'll post 
again.


