Every member in good standing in our database was sent a ballot in the last
election.  To be a member in good standing you must complete an annual audit
in some form.  That is achieved by either answering an annual audit form or
by participating in some way at the national level.  During this audit cycle
you are given up to 9 months to respond after your membership expires.
During that time you are treated like a normal member with one exception you
can't vote.  The 2700 "missing ballots" are individuals who are in this
status.  There are NO missing ballots.

Anyone who suggests that the status being unincorporated association is not
a problem clearly has chosen to ignore now public history.  When this User
Group went into court to pursue a case the case was thrown out within 6
weeks.  It was thrown on a motion that was filed by the other party that the
User Group lack standing to sue.  The membership of a unincorporated
association can sue for damages they actually experienced.  The association
itself cannot sue.  That means to sue each member must sue and if their is
any damage award it goes to member.  Additionally the award is NOT based on
the damages to the association. So if the association lost money but someone
could not show how that effected them personally there would be no damages
awarded.

Finally anyone who suggests we can just form a corporation without a bylaw
change is ignoring the not-for-profit tax issue at the federal level.

