In article <39EA4D6D.C356DCDE@pcde.inka.de>, Dennis Grevenstein <dennis@pcde.inka.de> writes:
:How can I copy the content of an Ultrix or VMS Installation CD
:on a tk 50 tape, so I can install the OS on an old VAX
:without SCSI?

  For OpenVMS VAX...  First create a standalone BACKUP tape, assuming
  that you have something running OpenVMS VAX around somewhere and can 
  use STABACKIT.COM to create the standalone BACKUP environment on TK50 
  media.  Then MOUNT the resulting tape and skip to the end of the tape, 
  and copy the VMS*.% kit files and then the DECW* files starting at the 
  end of the standalone BACKUP tape.  You have now created a tape that
  can be booted, and that (probably :-) has a valid copy of the key
  files from the distribution CD-ROM media.

  Alternatively, if you have a spare disk on the target system (that is 
  sufficiently large), you can create a tape containing standalone BACKUP 
  and then create a BACKUP saveset of the CD-ROM media onto the same tape 
  or onto a second tape.  Boot standalone BACKUP, and then restore the
  BACKUP of the distribution medium, then boot the restored copy and
  install from it.  (This will be the fastest, but it assumes that you 
  have a disk of at least 600 megabytes around -- some VAX systems do 
  have disks this large, and some do not.)

  If you have OpenVMS VAX installed on the target system, you can simply
  initialize a TK50 tape, copy out VMS*.% and DECW*.%, then perform a
  normal OpenVMS installation or (if the OpenVMS VAX version is within
  the window for upgrades) upgrade to the target release.

  You may/will need to transfer over other products, such as DECwindows 
  XUI or DECwindows Motif, TCP/IP Services, etc.

  I'd tend to look for an OpenVMS VAX system that has direct or served
  CD-ROM access, or acquire CD-ROM access for whichever VAX system this 
  is.  (If you indicate which specific VAX box, then I might be able to
  provide some tailored suggestions and hardware options.)

  OpenVMS VAX releases AFTER V7.3 will likely be available only on
  CD-ROM media, as the TK50 media itself is no longer particularly
  available -- TK50 and magtape media are thus likely to be retired.

  I do not know the equivilent sequence(s) for the ULTRIX distributions.

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




