antonio.carlini (arcarlini@iee.org) wrote:
: Chris Doran wrote:
: > The VT100 printset (MP00633), some of which may apply to the VT101, runs to
: > 60 sides of B3 when you include all the options. In the unlikely event that

: The VT101 is basically a VT100 without any options. I don't know whether
: anything was done to actually prevent the addition of options but if it
: was
: it's likely to have been components left off the boards and missing
: connectors and suchlike.

The VT100 and VT101 are very different animals inside the case.  The VT100
has the card cage and a power supply capable of powering the options that
slide into it.  The VT101 shares far more in common with the VT102 and is
essentially a VT102 with a number of components missing from the terminal
controller board.

You may have better luck looking at VT102 docs, however IIRC, the VT100
video hardware may be similar enough to the VT101 for your needs.

I had a similar problem with a VT100 years ago and on inspection I found
scorched components on the video board.  It may be sensible to replace the
video board entirely if the problem doesn't become obvious after checking
harnesses and pots.

Here are a couple of helpful URLs for more info:

http://www.cs.utk.edu/~shuford/terminal_index.html
http://www.vt100.net/

Hope your VT100 gets better!

