"NetBSD Bob" <nbsdbob@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> wrote
in message news:8s7jpk$ffi$1@uni00nw.unity.ncsu.edu...
> I am wanting to combine a TK70 as primary tape and a TK50 as
> secondary tape in an old MVII.  What switch settings do I need
> to set on the TQK50 card to do this, or is it just plug and play?

It is definitely not plug and play!

Configuring Q-BUS address and CSR Vectors can be very challenging.

Some devices have fixed addresses for the first or their kind, and floating
addresses for the others.  Some devices always have floating addresses.

Because of that, it is very difficult to set the addresses for some
configurations from just the manual.

If you have access to an OpenVMS system, you can run a configuration program
that is built in that will tell you what addresses to set each piece of
hardware to.

You must enter in every device that is on the Q-BUS.  And if you happen to
have any KFQSA boards, they actually pretend to be up to 7 Q-BUS devices,
the exact configuration of them must be entered into the configuration
program.

The configuration program is also built into the console rom of most VAXen
that are VAX 3500 or newer.  (I have heard of VAX 3500s that do not have
this program though).

If you do not have access to an OpenVMS system, I would suggest posting on
comp.os.vms a list of all of your devices that are on your Q-BUS, and
probably some one would run the configuration program for you to give you
the results.

Some also may have manuals, or URLs for manuals that can tell you what the
switch settings for the Q-BUS cards that you will need to change.

-John
wb8tyw@qsl.network





