Richard wrote:
> 
> On Sun, 08 Oct 2000 16:21:37 GMT, system@SendSpamHere.ORG (Brian
> Schenkenberger, VAXman-) wrote:
> 
> >I need to initialize to factory settings a DECbrouter 90 or I need to break
> >in to the password which has been established to reconfigure the device.
> 
> Is this one of the routers that gets it's config from a MOP load?  If so, you
> should be able to look at the config file in MOM$LOAD to find the password.  I
> had to do that on an old DEMSA-AA (MicroServer).


This is basically DEC hardware and Cisco IOS software (except it's
an old version V11 or so ... I don't think the DB90 has enough
memory to run V12 or later).

The only docs I can find to hand are on the Network Product Information
Library in DynaText format!

Anyway, this it what it tells you to do to recover a lost enable pwd:

1. Power cycle the box
2. Press BREAK within 60 seconds ... you should get a > prompt.
3. Type o (that's the letter not the number, I think) and note the
   value in the configuration register.
4. Type o/r which puts 0x41 into the config register.
5. Type i to init and boot the router.
6. Just say NO to everything and you should get to a prompt:
	Router(boot)>
7. Type enable to enter priv mode ... the prompt changes to:
	Router(boot)#>
   (note the hash ... it means you are in priv'ed mode).
8. Type show configuration
9. Restore the configuration register:
     Router(boot)# config-register 0xwhetever-hex-valueit-was
10. Type reload

If you have actually lost the console line password (I think that
means you cannot type anything at all into the console) then
there is a different procedure that starts "force the server
into factory diagnostic mode". I'll trawl the manuals looking for
how to do that if, and only if :-), the above is not enough.

Antonio

