<chunky10@my-deja.com> wrote in message
news:8rspiu$47a$1@nnrp1.deja.com...
> Unfortunately my predecessor did not leave any
> documentation for me to follow and I do not have
> any training on LAT, I can however get around the
> system. I have looked at the manuals but I want
> to be sure that I get it right first time!
>
Go to the SYS$COMMON:[SYSMGR] directory and see if there is a
LAT$SYSTARTUP.COM file.  If your predecessor did a clean VMS setup this
should be the file where LTA devices are defined.  If they aren't in
there, then you will have to hunt through the SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM file for
someplace that runs LATCP.  I've been called in on setups where the LAT
files were buried 4 or 5 layers deep in indirect COM files.  Try a
SEARCH on COM files for one of the LTA device names.

If you have DECNET you might want to delete the unused DECserver nodes
also.  Look in the SYS$COMMON:{DECSERVER] directories, if any exist, and
see if there is a DSVCONFIG.COM file.  Run this and delete the unused
decservers from the menu.
   Jack Peacock






