Derek,

today I managed to look into the directory [CONSOLE} of the PRO380.
It contains boot files BCIGEN.COM, BDAGEN.COM and CSAGEN.COM.
These are generic command procedures that boot the 8550 from an MSCP
disk on a CI server (HSCx0), a local controller (KDB50) and a local disk
of the PRO. The latter is a wild guess becaus I've never tried that myself.
But the PRO380 disks are called CSAn: as seen from VMS
( $ mc sysgen connect console)
So I doubt you can boot the 8530 from magtape.

Similarly named files are in that same directory, called BCIBOO.COM etc and
these are the ones actually called by the Boot command. The *GEN files
are called in turn by the *BOO files.

Our 8550 is not quite well anymore, while looking at the RD53 the VAX
suddenly
stopped working. Luckily it wasn't operational, but it could be an
indication that
the system is having problems. Could be that this VMS release (6.2) has
problems
with connecting console devices.
Our 8550 was built in 1989 (week 29) and bought by Fuji in 1991 as a
refurbished
system. It has been powered on ever since, and other than the problems of
today
never had any problem. Very reliable hardware. We kept it going, "we'll stop
the
maintenance contract and as soon as it dies we'll throw it out". Well that
happened
in 1995 or so :-)

Hans Vlems

