Hello,
    We've got a VAX 8530, and need to know how to boot it from tape.  We
have a TU81+ tape drive interfaced to the machine through it's own port
on the back.  The way the machine boots, is rather interesting.  First
you power it on and load the microcode from the console.  The "VAX
Console" is basically a Pro380 microcomputer with it's own special
interface to the machine.  Then, to boot the machine we run a script on
the console (like "DEFBOO.COM") which punches a bunch of values into the
machine's registers, then loads the bootloader ("VMB.EXE"), and passes
control to it.  The values you punch into the registers basically
determine what device the machine boots off of.  As we're missing the
"booting from tape" portion of our console manual, we basically need to
know what to put in our boot command file to boot the machine from the
TU81+.

Thanks,
    Derek Konigsberg
