From slot 5 onwards (i.e. leftwards) the Qbus follows a 
serpentine pattern. In slots 1-4 the grant is in the
top half only and the bottom half is not Qbus at all.
From slot 5 onwards the top half (A-B) is a Qbus slot and the
bottom half (C-D) is an independent Qbus slot.

The grant follows the following pattern:
	slot 5 top
	slot 5 bottom
	slot 6 bottom
	slot 6 top
	slot 7 top 
	slot 7 bottom
etc.

Something like this (if usenet doesn't eat it):

        7  6  5 

        .<..  ...<..
        .  .  .
        v  ^  v
        .  .  .
        .  .  .
     .<..  .<..


So from slot 5 onwards you must have no gaps in any sense 
i.e. if you have a dual-height card (like the RQDX3) in the 
top half of slot 6 there must be something in the bottom
half of slot 6 to feed in the grants.

Quad height cards usually get this right (but some can be
modified to work in BA200 cabs ... so things are not *that*
easy).

For the record BA23 cabs are similar but differ in where the pattern
starts and BA200 series are Qbus in AB and not Qbus (CD interconnect)
in slots CD all the way across.

Looking at your config I assume that you start off:

slot 1: M7606
slot 2: M7609
slot 3: M7609

otherwise something is seriously wrong (and there should be a
ribbon cable connecting these three).

In the top half of slot 4 you probably have the M3106 (DZQ11).
Anything in the bottom half of slot 4 won't work :-)

The M3107 (DHQ11) should be in the top half of slot 5.
The M7516 (DELQA) should be in the bottom half of slot 5.
The M7555 (RQDX3) should be in the bottom half of slot 6.
The M7559 (TQK70) should be in the top half of slot 6.

At least that is what I assume you meant when you said no gaps
(and I would swap the TQK70 and the RQDX3 but that's just me
being kind to the tape controller).

If you really meant some other order then you need to plug the gaps.

If you are unlucky then you already have this (or a similar
ordering) and you are now about to debug hardware :-)


