Bob, you're a scary man. I'm sure you'll be able to crowbar
NetBSD onto it if you try hard enough.

E&OE - this could be totally bogus.

DECsystem 5400 is the KN210 CPU board/IO board set which are Q-bus
quadcards, with their own private memory bus across the front,  via
the IDC50s. One of those is actually DSSI - the top one on the CPU board,
IIRC.

So, its a SPIM R3000A with DSSI, Ethernet and a few bits and pieces.
If its got BNC stuff (especially three) then its most likely for a 
framebuffer that does sync-on-green.

Just treat it as a big weird DECstation :)

